    "updated_at": "2022-12-01T11:43:21Z",
    "body": "Hmm. I think without the controls attribute, the audio element is invisible, and so is more like a script element. If we say that the element creating something hearable is the only requirement, then we'd have to say that script elements which use the web audio API are palpable content.\r\n\r\nAnd I don't think it's really about \"visible\" vs. \"invisible\", actually, i.e. this isn't sighted-medium specific. It's about whether the element provides useful content to any user, and thus can make the surrounding element feel palpable, vs. whether it's just doing something functional, and could in theory be placed anywhere in the DOM.\r\n\r\nSo I think the current spec's restriction here is correct.",
